WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Your cells keep their genetic
instructions locked away inside a

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.670
nucleus.

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.610
A bacterium has no nucleus at all.

4
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.450
Yet it still carries every
instruction it needs to live.

5
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.350
So where does a
bacterium keep its DNA,

6
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.550
and what else does it manage without?

7
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.750
In this mission, you'll meet
the parts that animal and plant

8
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.190
cells share: the nucleus, cytoplasm,

9
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.200
cell membrane and mitochondria.

10
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.970
You'll find the three extra
parts that plant cells have and

11
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.830
animal cells don't.

12
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.110
Then you'll look inside
a bacterial cell,

13
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.730
and see how its DNA is arranged,

14
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.350
including tiny extra
rings called plasmids.

15
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.770
Your mission: find out where
a bacterium keeps its DNA.
